From: iOSPlus10 display-perf agent
Subject: [PATCH] negroni fb: vsync after the frame, clock shift inside the copy (0267)

Measured (log 2026-10-26 13:18-13:31, kernel local-20261026-074105, config args):
swaps/s 40-80, presents/s 28-70, copy avg 2.1-2.6 ms / max 6-8 ms, swapwait busy
answers 60-417/s. The copy time is mostly the 0256 wait for the GPU copy's fence before
the CPU clock shift, and the tick sent the vsync notification before that: CoreAnimation
woke on it, asked SwapWait for the swap the tick was still copying, retried for 1 ms and
skipped the heartbeat. The shift itself read the write-combined panel memory (uncached,
~10 MB/s: 0265 measured ~1 s per full-screen read pass) for 120 x 540 pixels while the
display engine scanned it: the top-left strip shows half-shifted and unshifted rows.

1. negronifb_notifylate (default 1): with the display on, the tick queues its frame,
   publishes the swap id, then notifies; the CPU drawing over a GPU copy (presentFinish:
   the 0256 shift, badges) runs after the notification. 0 = the old order.
2. negronifb_clockcopy (default 1): a one-layer frame that covers the strip is written
   already shifted: GPU = 4 rectangles in one submission (NegroniGPUPresentRects, one IB,
   one fence), CPU = 3 memcpys per strip row. The n pixels opened at the left edge get the n
   pixels pushed out at the middle (the notch area, no status bar item); 0256 used the edge
   pixel of each row. Zero-copy (0234) fills the same way. 0 = the 0256 behaviour.
Host test: patches/xnu/tests/fb-clock-copy-test.c (rectangles and CPU rows vs a reference).

